SUMMARY:Aga Khan Museum:  Labyrinth Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n( SOLD-OUT )\n\nWe will return to see 
 **Labyrinth Ensemble** for the 5th time!\n\n[https://www.labyrinthontario.
 com/s/stories/labyrinth-ensemble-with-efren-lopez-2](https://www.labyrinth
 ontario.com/s/stories/labyrinth-ensemble-with-efren-lopez-2)\n\nEvery FOUR
  years\, the 14 members 'disband'\, and a new group of 14 members is put t
 ogether. A new cohort!\n\nWhich also means 14 new instruments to learn abo
 ut!\n\nThe new cohort will dig into European Medieval\, the Eastern Medite
 rranean\, the Middle East\, and Central Asian musical traditions\, and wil
 l feature unique instrumentation ranging from guzheng\, Hardanger fiddle\,
  lutes\, hurdy gurdy\, qanun and microtonal guitar\; bringing a whole new 
 sound to the project.\n\nThe Aga Khan Museum concert venue is one of our t
 op 3 spots in Toronto--for live music.\n\nTickets have just gone 'on sale'
 . I've purchased a ticket in Row F.\n\nPrices are: $50 regular. $37.50 for
  Senior.\n\nhttps://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/labyrinth-with-efren-lopez/
 \n\n\\*\\*\\*Purchase your own ticket--**and the ticket price includes** e
 ntry into the Museum from 6pm onwards (which we always do). We can check o
 ut the new exhibitions.\n\nIf interested\, grab your own ticket. Don't mis
 s out!\n\nA short video--3 of the 14 members perform at local Thorncliffe 
 Park festival last summer\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o2XjudW45nQ
