SUMMARY:Women in Musical Leadership Masterclass with the TSO: Conducting (
 FREE)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWhat exactly is Conducting?\n\n--How d
 oes one learn to Conduct?\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-Could you be an **Orchestra Condu
 ctor**? Interpret a score with your gestures and verbal cues!!\n\nRegister
  for your **FREE** ticket (below)---\n\nWe've attended this in PAST years-
 -with FAB turnout/INTEREST..\n\nhttps://tapestryopera.com/performances/wom
 en-in-musical-leadership-masterclass-2/\n\nCreated and run by **Tapestry O
 pera**\, with **lead partner the Toronto Symphony Orchestra\,** *Women in 
 Musical Leadership* is a three-year program designed to collectively devel
 op the next generation of women and non-binary conductors and music direct
 ors in Canada.\nWomen in Musical Leadership Conductors work with **Maestro
  Gustavo** **Gimeno** and the musicians of the Toronto Symphony Orchestra 
 in this Masterclass held at Roy Thomson Hall.\n\n\\*\\*\\*During this mast
 erclass\, you will observe Women In Musical Leadership Conductors **Monica
  Chen** and **Eve Legault**\, and Associate Conductor **Serena Reuten** wo
 rk with TSO Music Director **Gustavo Gimeno** and the world-class TSO. It
 ’s a unique experience that always reveals fascinating details of the co
 nductors’ craft and offers a peek “behind the scenes” of an orchestr
 a’s rehearsal process.\n\nFREE ticket link here--(please attend if you r
 eserve a ticket)\n\nhttps://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#
 /events/a0SOF0000024Ba12AE\n\nNOTE: this is the SATURDAY morning of the MA
 Y long weekend.\n\nCoffee/chat before or afterwards!
